{{slim-wikipedia|Xerxes|Xerxes (disambiguation)}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|grc|Ξέρξης}}, from {{der|en|peo|𐎧𐏁𐎹𐎠𐎼𐏁𐎠||ruler among kings|tr=Xšayāršā}}. {{doublet|en|Ahasuerus}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/ˈzɜk.siːz/|lang=en}}
* {{a|US}} {{enPR|zûrk'sēz}}, {{IPA|/ˈzɝksiːz/|lang=en}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun|es}}

# [[w:Xerxes_I_of_Persia|Xerxes I]], a Persian king of the Achaemenid dynasty who reigned 485-465 BC.
# [[w:Xerxes_II_of_Persia|Xerxes II]], a Persian king who ruled for 45 days in 424 BC before being assassinated.
# {{non-gloss definition|{{given name|lang=en|male|from=Old Persian}} mainly applied to historical and fictional characters.}}

